# Project Overview
This is a Flutter Web portfolio application connected to a Supabase PostgreSQL backend.

# Tech Stack
- Frontend: Flutter (Web optimized), Dart
- Backend: Supabase (PostgreSQL, Authentication)
- Deployment: GitHub Actions (CI/CD) to Cloud Storage

# Coding Conventions
- Use modular, reusable Flutter widgets (e.g., keep Hero, ProjectGrid, and Experience in separate files).
- Keep state management lightweight to ensure optimal web load times.
- Ensure all UI components are mobile-first and fully responsive.
- Write optimized PostgreSQL queries for the Supabase integration to prevent UI lag.

# Rules & Anti-Patterns
- Never generate raw HTML/CSS/JS; always use the Flutter framework equivalents.
- Avoid heavy, third-party animation packages; rely on Flutter's built-in implicit animations and `AnimationController`.
- Prioritize SEO and accessibility best practices in the `web/index.html` wrapper before the Flutter engine initializes.
- When generating SQL, always include Row Level Security (RLS) policies.